{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adcb-472d-71a1-881f-1812150e91d5"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"74587b85-895b-4603-8919-047353d70d11","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"74587b85-895b-4603-8919-047353d70d11","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"74587b85-895b-4603-8919-047353d70d11"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(TASK-260830-2f5393, status=integrating)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\nRun `task-board spawn directives \"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\"` at safe checkpoints,\nat most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.\nDirectives have no delivery timer.\nSave before cancel; pause/reroute safely.\nIf reading directives fails, report unknown; do not treat it as none.\n\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `developer` (`implementer`) — Writes code, fixes bugs, writes tests\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use scoped board projections; skip `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `swiftui`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/swiftui/SKILL.md`\n- `core-data`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/core-data/SKILL.md`\n- `go-testing-tools`: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.claude/skills/go-testing-tools/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Implement lease creation, renewal, expiry policy, epoch monotonicity, holder identity, and compare-and-swap writes\n- [ ] Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\n- [ ] README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\n- [ ] Implementation matches AC\n- [ ] Solution fits project architecture\n- [ ] Tests green\n- [ ] Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\n- [ ] If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260830-2f5393\n- **Title:** TASK-260830-2f5393: implement-lease-record-validation-and-cas\n- **Parent:** STORY-260830-1oqfec\n\n### Description\n\nImplement lease creation, renewal, expiry policy, epoch monotonicity, holder identity, and compare-and-swap writes. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\n\n### Scope\n\nrelux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); §2.2, §5.3, §13.6-13.10. Work only inside the ownership-leases-and-fencing story boundary.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nProduction behavior demonstrates: Implement lease creation, renewal, expiry policy, epoch monotonicity, holder identity, and compare-and-swap writes. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260830-2f5393_producer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2f5393/TASK-260830-2f5393_producer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `4816`\n- Content digest: `sha256:ae9f35f6e0af859f6f2418b8a945d790713cbf8af36f749220f6ebaae7daf6f5`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-2f5393_reviewer-cr1.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2f5393/TASK-260830-2f5393_reviewer-cr1.md`\n\n- Byte count: `6775`\n- Content digest: `sha256:049162b26da418deabecca30d9d19d8c75ce1783cb1467d9eab97fae6f0e3a3e`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-2f5393_checkpoint-brief-rev1.md\nCheckpoint-only run for TASK-260830-2f5393 (implement-lease-record-validation-and-cas, STORY-260830-1oqfec). Change Request revision 1 was ACCEPTED by the independent reviewer RUN-260917-c46f34 (TASK-260830-2f5393_review-verdict-rev1.md, the CR-TASK-260830-2f5393-1 candidate tree on base 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e); the leaf is a non-final Story leaf (siblings TASK-260830-3g12yp and TASK-260830-2atgj4 follow), so the accepted candidate must become one internal signed checkpoint commit on the Story branch and the task must remain integrating. Do exactly this, from the control root /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager with the authoritative board: (1) read the board state (task integrating, CR rev1 accepted, checklist complete) and the verdict; (2) run `task-board worktree checkpoint TASK-260830-2f5393` (this run is the producer-bound integration run the command requires) and record its exact output and exit; (3) verify the result: `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree verify-commit HEAD` good signature for oparin@me.com, the commit's tree equals the accepted CR tree, its parent is 62d4463, `git status` in the Story worktree is clean apart from the board checkout artifact, `task-board worktree status` shows the CR checkpointed and the task integrating with integrationCheckpointed=true; (4) attach TASK-260830-2f5393_checkpoint-rev1.md as a task-scoped outcome with every command, exit code and OID; then exit. Do NOT change the task status, do NOT make product changes, do NOT commit manually, do NOT integrate or land the Story, do NOT run a generic handoff, do NOT rerun product suites (accept the immutable review evidence; claim no executions you did not perform). If the checkpoint command refuses, attach the refusal verbatim in the outcome and exit non-zero without any repair attempt. Model: muse-spark max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260830-2f5393_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260830-2f5393, name=TASK-260830-2f5393_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `integrating` is the role handoff status; use it only after the evidence contract is satisfied.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff TASK-260830-2f5393 --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260830-1oqfec.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-1oqfec`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n\n## Integration Assignment\n\nThis is the integration run for accepted Change Request `CR-TASK-260830-2f5393-1` revision 1. The immutable producer binding is role `developer` (archetype `implementer`). Keep the board at `integrating`; only the integration transaction may write `done`. This assignment supersedes generic producer FIRST/LAST status and handoff instructions: run the bound checkpoint or integration command, attach fresh task-scoped outcome evidence, then end without calling the generic `handoff` command or setting status yourself.\n"}}
